I'm afraid I don't use Fishpool, but here are some general points to 
telnet playing:

tom@no.com wrote:
> i logged into hal.pp.fishpool.fi, got vt100 to run,
> but wasnt able to find the switch for the alt key,
> which enable things like ALT-A for adjust.

Hm; I think you are stuck with using the "#" versions.  This is entirely 
up to the server with regards to what it does with special keys like Alt 
and AltGr.

> as for graphics, if i want another symbol for
> a corridor, do i really need to pass the 
> whole graphic set to change # to . ?

You might need to change your Code Page to 437 (Choose CP437 from 
Window->Translation) - this is the character set with the weird IBM 
graphics symbols (IBMGraphics).

(Ensure you are using a version of PuTTY after 0.51 for this)

Don't you forget to enable IBMGraphics in the Nethack options, mind.

> i dont suppose that its possible, to have
> the nice windows font on these servers ??

Certainly;  In PuTTY, set your terminal font to whatever you choose;  
FixedSys seems to be a good choice if you want it to look like the 
Nethack-in-a-DOS-box incarnation (Lucida Console is another quite good 
one (Size 14 whilst big is quite nice looking): sadly you cannot simply 
use the built-in Windows Raster Fonts with PuTTY).

Lastly, if the server supports colour xterms, you can set your terminal 
type as "xterm-color" in PuTTY and then enable the option 'color' in 
Nethack...

